  <compounddef id="conceptscl_1_1feature_1_1concepts_1_1executor" kind="concept">
    <compoundname>scl::feature::concepts::executor</compoundname>
    <includes refid="concepts_2executor_8h" local="no">executor.h</includes>
    <templateparamlist>
      <param>
        <type>typename Type</type>
      </param>
    </templateparamlist>
    <initializer>template&lt;typename Type&gt;
concept <ref refid="conceptscl_1_1feature_1_1concepts_1_1executor" kindref="compound">scl::feature::concepts::executor</ref> =  <ref refid="group__scl__feature__type__traits_1ga4b4a83fa2f91118b959d5566a2a782c7" kindref="member">::scl::feature::is_executor_v</ref>&lt;Type&gt;    </initializer>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Satisfied when <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> implements the executor interface. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An executor is a class template that defines the storage strategy and access policy for an <computeroutput>scl::wrapper</computeroutput>. <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> must provide the following static methods, callable for <computeroutput>Type&amp;</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>Type&amp;&amp;</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> const&amp;:</para>
<para><table rows="3" cols="2"><row>
<entry thead="yes"><para>Method   </para>
</entry><entry thead="yes"><para>Role    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>value(Self&amp;&amp;)</computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Returns a reference to the held value.    </para>
</entry></row>
<row>
<entry thead="no"><para><computeroutput>execute(Self&amp;&amp;, Func&amp;&amp;)</computeroutput>   </para>
</entry><entry thead="no"><para>Invokes a callable in executor&apos;s context.   </para>
</entry></row>
</table>
</para>
<para>Optional methods (<computeroutput>guard</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>unguard</computeroutput>) may be provided to implement RAII locking; their presence is detected separately via <computeroutput>is_guard_noexcept_v</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>is_unguard_noexcept_v</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>cv-ref qualifiers on <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> are stripped before the check (<computeroutput>remove_cvref_t</computeroutput>).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type to check.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
